            "is_markdown": true,
            "count": 0,
            "text": "Created attachment 3642\nALTREP-aware objectsize function.\n\nFor example:\n\n```\n> x <- 1:1e12\n> format(object.size(x), units = \"auto\")\n[1] \"7.3 Tb\"\n```\n\nWhether this is correct, I guess, is a matter of perspective -- the actual current size of this object is far smaller thanks to the compact ALTREP representation, but certain operations could still force materialization of this into a vector that would be 7.3 Tb in size.\n\nA minimal proposed patch; note that I omit the size of `ALTREP_CLASS(x)` here. I also include null checks as I'm not certain if there are guarantees that the altrep data for an object are non-null.\n\n```\nIndex: src/library/utils/src/size.c\n===================================================================\n--- src/library/utils/src/size.c\t(revision 89685)\n+++ src/library/utils/src/size.c\t(working copy)\n@@ -44,6 +44,18 @@\n     SEXP tmp, dup;\n     bool isVec = false;\n \n+    if (ALTREP(s)) {\n+\tSEXP data1 = R_altrep_data1(s);\n+\tSEXP data2 = R_altrep_data2(s);\n+\tcnt += sizeof(SEXPREC);\n+\tif (data1 != NULL && data1 != R_NilValue)\n+\t    cnt += objectsize(data1);\n+\tif (data2 != NULL && data2 != R_NilValue)\n+\t    cnt += objectsize(data2);\n+\tcnt += objectsize(ATTRIB(s));\n+\treturn(cnt);\n+    }\n+\n     switch (TYPEOF(s)) {\n     case NILSXP:\n \treturn(0);\n```",
            "bug_id": 19028,
            "creator": "kevinushey",
            "creation_time": "2026-03-24T19:00:53Z"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
